<article className={"prose"}><p className={"opening"}>{"Zero is a rolling, updating blog on development, features, and implementations. We're VERY much under construction, but signup and profiles are live and more features and refinement roll out every day."}</p> <h2>{"What’s the big idea?"}</h2> <p>{"Honestly, I hate almost everything the internet has become in the time I’ve been around "}<em>{"(56k modem plays softly in the background)"}</em>{". Making connections online has moved from the backrooms and seedy chat apps and parents warning you that you might be talking to a 40yo man to the forefront of what people used the internet for to back to seedy chat apps about The Backrooms (2026) where you seek out 40yo men. Every login is a Fuck You. Every site wants your data, your unique identifier, they want to sell you something or sell you to someone and the entire experience on the open web feels like rawdogging a bonzibuddy taskbar install. "}<u>{"It doesn’t have to be like this"}</u>{". Ok Cupid was great and I want it back. Do you?"}</p> <h2>{"Spite."}</h2> <p>{"It’s 100% spite and 10% nostalgia."}</p> <p>{"I’m obviously not a Harvard math major like the old crew."}</p> <p>{"I’m just a guy that’s tired of having to accept dogshit. Theoretically, I can take the fight to the apps not by complaining about how much they suck and "}<em>{"asking"}</em>{" for redress but by making an alternative. "}<EditorialLink href={"https://nightrider.onrender.com/hub"}>{"I have a history of doing exactly that."}</EditorialLink>{" As long as I can avoid a C&D from OKC, I plan on doing what they did, but better."}</p> <h2>{"The Other Players"}</h2> <p><EditorialLink href={"https://duolicious.app/"}>{"Duolicious"}</EditorialLink>{" seems to be killing it these days, BUT I havent been on since normies discovered it and it blew up years ago, until recently. Shit was a straight up strawberry femcel farm where you picked your own. They're still missing a \"last seen online\" feature past 24 hours but they're already doing most of what I want to do with this, other than being incredibly zoomer coded."}</p> <p><EditorialLink href={"https://www.cercadating.com/"}>{"Cerca"}</EditorialLink>{", yet another incredibly zoomer coded app. This one all but explicitly catering to yuppies that already have a rich social life. Bro if you have 5 friends and live in a major city why the fuck are you on a dating app, you already have a life."}</p> <p>{"The current "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.okcupid.com/"}>{"OKC"}</EditorialLink>{" somehow would STILL today be the best option if it wasnt for Duo and their own greed."}</p> <p>{"I can't imagine the rest of the big names have changed anything for the better."}</p> <h2>{"The little ideas"}</h2> <p>{"You already got the nickel tour on the landing page. Here’s what else I have in mind:"}</p> <ul className={"manifesto-list"}> <li>{"All moderation gets human sign off. All. Nobody gets their shit deleted without knowing why. Nobody gets shadowbanned because they said the word “cyber”. Wanna post a pic with a gun, a dead fish, your much hotter friends, go ahead. As long as it isn't illegal or opens us up to litigation, go ham. Even then, if it’s funny, we might leave it up anyways."}</li> <li>{"Premium features will always be obtainable without paying TWICE. More on that later."}</li> <li>{"The purpose of the site is to get you out there, meeting people IRL. Everything here should serve that first, and cover hosting second. I don’t care if this shit makes me a penny. This is about spite, love, and making something cool. The moment this project deviates from that, blow my shit smoove off."}</li> <li>{"True matchmaking algos based on data YOU enter. Nothing black box. Answer the questions, enter weights for others’ answers. That’s as deep as it gets."}</li> <li>{"Premium features and paywall don’t make the site unusable if you don’t have them."}</li> <li>{"References from friends and former partners (see "}<EditorialLink href={"/ogtrends/references/"}>{"OKTrends #2"}</EditorialLink>{")."}</li> <li>{"Community voting for good and bad profiles, and we'll do a monthly showcase of the site's 3 best and worst."}</li> <li>{"In-app chat with pics, but the pic feature doesn't unlock until both parties send 3 messages. Nothing will be scraped or moderated unless somebody in the convo flags it."}</li> </ul> <h3>{"What's being worked on now"}</h3> <ol className={"manifesto-list"}> <li>{"Backend alignment of the current bank of 410 match questions to personality traits, and getting personality awards and badges rolled out."}</li> <li>{"A historical fact-finding dig into the original Dating Persona Test questions and answers, and integrating that data with a modern revamp and new personas."}</li> <li>{"Overall site polish and spaghetti-code unravelling (yeah, the whole thing is vibe coded, for now)."}</li> </ol> <p className={"founder-announcement"}><strong>{"THE FIRST 250 PROFILES GET TRIPLE OG STATUS FOR LIFE"}</strong>{"And a special Founder Profile badge in their personality awards."}</p> <h2>{"Premium"}</h2> <p>{"We call it OG status. With it, you get unlimited messaging and exclusive features like references. Without it, you have to take the Dating Persona Test (up now in beta), answer 250 match questions, and have a fully fleshed out profile with pictures and everything, then you can message OG status users if they message you first or send the first message if your match% is over 97%."}</p> <p>{"To get it, it costs 3 Bucks."}</p> <p><strong>{"To keep it, you have to do everything above, and either respond to 25% of messages received or get a 25% response rate on messages sent AND send or receive 4 messages a month, and it’s free after that. Never pay again. ALL features, nothing behind separate paywalls. I think that’s fair. Look at what the other guys are charging for far less:"}</strong></p> <div className={"pricing-scroll"} role={"region"} aria-label={"Dating app pricing comparison"} tabIndex={"0"}> <table className={"competitor-pricing"}> <thead><tr><th scope={"col"}>{"App"}</th><th scope={"col"}>{"Lowest paid tier"}</th><th scope={"col"}>{"Reported U.S. price"}</th><th scope={"col"}>{"What that gets you"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Tinder"}</th><td>{"Plus"}</td><td><strong>{"$9.99*"}</strong></td><td>{"Unlimited likes and rewinds, Passport location changes, fewer ads."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Plenty of Fish"}</th><td>{"POF Plus"}</td><td><strong>{"$19.99/mo"}</strong></td><td>{"Unlimited likes, extended profiles, incognito browsing, no ads."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Grindr"}</th><td>{"XTRA"}</td><td><strong>{"$14.99–$22.99*"}</strong></td><td>{"No third-party ads, up to 500 profiles, read receipts, Grindr Web."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Bumble"}</th><td>{"Boost"}</td><td><strong>{"$29.99–$39.99/mo"}</strong></td><td>{"Unlimited likes, Backtrack, Rematch, Extend, Spotlight/SuperSwipe allowances."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"OkCupid"}</th><td>{"Premium"}</td><td><strong>{"$34.99/mo"}</strong></td><td>{"See who likes you, unlimited likes, dealbreakers, more match-question access."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Match"}</th><td>{"Basic / Standard"}</td><td><strong>{"$44.99/mo"}</strong></td><td>{"Unlimited likes, rewinds, expanded discovery."}</td></tr> <tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Hinge"}</th><td>{"Hinge+"}</td><td><strong>{"$49.99/mo"}</strong></td><td>{"Unlimited likes, advanced preferences, see all incoming likes together."}</td></tr> </tbody></table></div> <p className={"pricing-note"}><strong>{"U.S. pricing snapshot, November 2026."}</strong>{" Monthly figures reflect reported single-month options, not discounted long-term plans. *Tinder Plus and Grindr XTRA amounts are publicly listed in-app purchases whose billing periods aren't specified in the listing. Actual prices vary by location, age, platform, promotion and term. Sources: "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.datingapi.io/insights/dating-app-subscription-prices"}>{"U.S. App Store price index"}</EditorialLink>{", "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.datingscout.com/bumble/review"}>{"Bumble"}</EditorialLink>{", "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.datingscout.com/hinge/review"}>{"Hinge"}</EditorialLink>{", "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.datingscout.com/okcupid/review"}>{"OkCupid"}</EditorialLink>{", and "}<EditorialLink href={"https://www.forbes.com/health/dating/plenty-of-fish-review/"}>{"POF"}</EditorialLink>{"."}</p><nav className={"article-nav"} aria-label={"Article links"}><EditorialLink href={"/ogtrends/"}>{"← All OgTrends"}</EditorialLink><EditorialLink href={"/ogtrends/perfect-profile/"}>{"Next: The Perfect Dating Profile →"}</EditorialLink></nav></article>
